  },
  {
    "text": "QFI serves as a momentum-resolved probe of entanglement, offering a novel perspective on quantum critical phenomena beyond being a lower bound for entanglement depth.",
    "topic": "QFI as a Probe of Quantum Critical Phenomena"
  },
  {
    "text": "When emergent quantum phases in frustrated spin systems are approached, QFI diverges across multiple wave vectors in momentum space.",
    "topic": "QFI Divergence in Frustrated Spin Systems"
  },
  {
    "text": "In antiferromagnets with a zero-energy Goldstone mode, linear spin wave theory breaks down and QFI (and entanglement depth) diverges at the magnetic ordering wave vector.",
